      "verdict": "Conditional design is coherent after both precision comments were incorporated in EN and RU. D1 is still open; this review does not authorize or mark a production implementation ready.",
      "decision": "A: reject native-eligible propertyless targets before allocation in the default adapter (recommended), or B: explicitly design eager behavior for higher-level callers.",
      "boundaries_reviewed": [
        "Default native adapter owns detection; no global limit on alternate implementations.",
        "Complete parent-chain scan includes private backed slots; static-only and virtual-only do not qualify.",
        "stdClass and inherited backed properties distinguished from other internal classes.",
        "Naive eager proxy fallback changes timing, product identity and destroys an unused ordinary placeholder.",
        "ClassDefinition remains eager; existing before-instantiation application effects are not promised rollback.",
        "Supported direct callbacks keep deferred execution and original later exception identity.",
        "The default native factory boundary preserves alternate/custom factories and ordinary eager ClassDefinition behavior."
      ],
